Description: An R implementation of the Stata 'slopepower' command of Nash,
    Morgan, Frost and Mulick (2021) <doi:10.1177/1536867X211045512>. Performs
    sample size and power calculations for two-arm parallel trials in which the
    outcome is a rate of change (slope) estimated by a linear mixed model.
    Parameters are estimated in a first stage from previously collected
    longitudinal data, or supplied directly, and combined in a second stage with
    the design of a proposed trial. The model is fixed and narrow: one
    continuous outcome, a straight line in time, a random intercept and random
    slope per participant, and a treatment effect that is a difference in
    slopes. Participants are assumed independent, so there is no adjustment for
    covariates, no further level of clustering such as site, and no
    randomisation scheme other than two equal parallel arms.
